@startuml
title dep — Trusted ingress boundary (accepted 2026-10-13)
node "Visitor device" as Visitor
node "Operator-controlled host" as Host {
  node "TLS edge" as Edge
  node "Private frontend network" as Front {
    node "Nginx container\nfixed trusted API peer" as Nginx
    node "Express API container\nno published port" as API
  }
  artifact "Read-only trusted-ingress.conf\nexact observed edge peer" as Config
  node "Private database network" as Back {
    database "MongoDB\nno published port" as DB
  }
}
Visitor --> Edge : HTTPS\nPII: client IP\nSensitive: session / credentials
Edge --> Nginx : Existing loopback ingress path\nPII: overwritten client-IP header
Config ..> Nginx : required configuration mount
Nginx --> API : canonical client IP\nexisting session / auth payload
API --> DB : existing session / application IO
note right of Nginx
  No automatic broad network trust.
  Untrusted or unusable identity -> 403.
  Health check remains on root path.
end note
note bottom of Host
  Host administrator remains trusted.
  NAT may change the observed peer address.
  This correction grants no transport-policy exception
  and does not authorize production deployment.
end note
@enduml
